y  the gene variant so if you're looking  for a specific  mutation that a target a therapy is  targeted to  this database allows you to find  multiple models typically with a  specific genetic mutation for those drug  testing studies  so if i click on in this case a bladder  tumor example you see what comes up here  is an entire list of different tumors  that are available in the database with  patient information and also um some  information on the genetic makeup of the  tumor if i pick one of these  and click on it  and we dig down deeper and really see  what's available for each of these  tumors that is there's a patient  information  there are gene  uh  excuse me copy number variation gene  varied information growth characteristic  characteristics and all the genomic  information we have so again you can  just go publicly available website at  jackson laboratory and and review all  this information  uh also connected with each tumor we we  have what's shown here is the gene  expression it's called the z number  whether it's an over express or under  expresser of specific genes  and we also make available something  called copy number variation that looks  at the representation of specific genes  in the genome whether there are  more copies than normal or fewer copies  than normal  another aspect of our program here which  is quite unique is the way that  researchers can access these models  we provide and we're really one of the  only uh laboratories that provide what  are called study ready cohorts that is  these are mice that we have engrafted  with tumors characterized and we will  ship to any researcher that allow them  to do drug efficacy studies or other  basic biology studies so any of the  solid tumors we have in the tumor  database  we have some aml models that are very  popular that's acute myeloid leukemia  these are engrafted with  myelo leukemia cells that are isolated  from individual patients and are used to  develop anti-leukemia drugs  and we a